invariant: INV-17
file: sha512.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: a host object's compress_blocks wipes the stack below it before it
  calls its compression function and not after, so that function's dead
  frame keeps the last sixteen words of the last block's message
  schedule, and whichever working variables its compiler wrote to slots
  of its own. Under HMAC-SHA-384 the first block is the key, and the
  schedule's words give back the block. Every digest is still right, so
  no vector sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test paints the stack, makes each
  kind of call on sha512.c's first arm, and requires no word the call
  computed in the bytes it wrote.

--- old
    COMPRESS_BLOCKS(h, p, blocks);
    wipe_frame_call();
--- new
    wipe_frame_call();
    COMPRESS_BLOCKS(h, p, blocks);
